\details{
Unofficial, keyless API, not supported by Euroleague Basketball; hoopR only
wraps it (wrap-only: payloads are not redistributed as release assets). This
function mirrors sdv-py's \code{euroleague_game_points()}: same arguments,
defaults and snake_case columns, one row per sdv-py row.

\strong{Coordinate frame}, as measured in the reference capture (E2025 game 1,
158 rows; U2025 game 1, 176 rows):
\itemize{
\item \strong{Units: integer centimeters. Origin: the hoop.} 2FG radii run 8-512 cm,
3FG radii 722-925 cm (the FIBA arc is 675 cm), zone \code{A} (rim) sits at
radius 8-33 cm.
\item \strong{Both teams are mapped onto one basket; \code{coord_y} grows away from the
baseline toward the court} (-6 to 865 cm for every team on the E game,
-69 to 1028 on the U game; 3FG rows sit at y 414-865). Negative y is
behind the hoop (the U game has a few rows up to 69 cm behind it, i.e.
under or behind the backboard).
\item \code{coord_x} is signed left / right of the hoop (-683 to 696 cm); 3-point
zone \code{H} is x < 0 and \code{I} is x > 0. Which sideline is positive (from the
shooter's view or from the scorer's table) is \strong{UNVERIFIED} from the data
alone.
\item \strong{Free throws are not located}: \code{FTM} rows carry \code{coord_x = coord_y = -1}
and \code{zone = ""} (a sentinel, not a spot 1 cm from the hoop). Filter them
out before plotting.
\item \code{zone} letters A-I: A rim, B / C close left / right, D / E mid, F / G long
two, H / I three.
}

The live API's codes are space-padded fixed-width strings
(\code{TEAM = "IST       "}); every string cell is stripped. Its "no such game"
answer is an \strong{empty 200 body}, returned as a zero-row tibble with the
documented columns (not an error). A 404 raises \code{hoopR_no_data}, a 400 / 422
\code{hoopR_invalid_request}, any other failure \code{hoopR_fetch_error} (all inherit
\code{hoopR_error}).
